=3D"figure-image max-h-[42cqi]">
  </a>

<!---->  </figure>

</div><p>Securing your endpoints is markedly different than securing your n=
etwork. In legacy network architectures, you can use your network to protec=
t your endpoints. That strategy is less useful in modern, mobile, and cloud=
-based environments because you cannot guarantee that your endpoints will a=
lways be behind your network. As your corporate endpoints connect to busine=
ss partner networks, to hosted environments, and to other networks that you=
 do not control, you must focus on protecting the endpoint independently of=
 protecting the network. Both are important and both must be addressed.</p>=
<p>This training explains how Cisco Secure Endpoint protects your endpoints=
 and how to implement and manage Cisco Secure Endpoint solutions.</p><div i=
d=3D"ember88">         =20
  <figure class=3D"figure">
<!---->   =20
  <a href=3D"https://ondemandelearning.cisco.com/apollo-alpha/sec-scor-34-a=
mpforendpoints-20/assets/Security/Modular/SCOR/v2.0/Graphics/Course34/SCOR_=
2-0-0_Deploying_Cisco_AMP_for_Endpoints_Learning_Experience_001.png" rel=3D=
"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank" class=3D"transition-opacity hover:o=
pacity-75 focus:opacity-75">
    <img src=3D"https://ondemandelearning.cisco.com/apollo-alpha/sec-scor-3=
4-ampforendpoints-20/assets/Security/Modular/SCOR/v2.0/Graphics/Course34/SC=
OR_2-0-0_Deploying_Cisco_AMP_for_Endpoints_Learning_Experience_001.png" cla=
ss=3D"figure-image max-h-[42cqi]">
  </a>

<!---->  </figure>

</div><p>This training provides videos, reading materials, and examples to =
help you learn Cisco Secure Endpoint. It includes hands-on simulated lab ex=
ercises that allow you to explore the Cisco Secure Endpoint console and the=
n use it to perform endpoint analysis to help you to see for yourself how C=
isco Secure Endpoint defends against ransomware.</p><p>The training also in=
cludes review questions that will allow you to test your knowledge and unde=
rstanding.</p><div id=3D"ember89">         =20
  <figure class=3D"figure">
<!---->   =20
  <a href=3D"https://ondemandelearning.cisco.com/apollo-alpha/sec-scor-34-a=
mpforendpoints-20/assets/Security/Modular/SCOR/v2.0/Graphics/Course34/SCOR_=
2-0-0_Deploying_Cisco_AMP_for_Endpoints_Challenges_and_Opportunities_001.pn=
g" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank" class=3D"transition-opacit=
y hover:opacity-75 focus:opacity-75">
    <img src=3D"https://ondemandelearning.cisco.com/apollo-alpha/sec-scor-3=
4-ampforendpoints-20/assets/Security/Modular/SCOR/v2.0/Graphics/Course34/SC=
OR_2-0-0_Deploying_Cisco_AMP_for_Endpoints_Challenges_and_Opportunities_001=
.png" class=3D"figure-image max-h-[42cqi]">
  </a>

<!---->  </figure>

</div><p>Cisco Secure Endpoint accelerates security response by providing v=
isibility and clarity to previously unknown artifacts in exchanged files, a=
nd by seeing a threat once and blocking it everywhere. The technology that =
is used by Cisco Secure Endpoint is called Cisco Advanced Malware Protectio=
n (AMP) and is available both on network devices and on endpoints, thus add=
ressing security both of network and endpoints. In the context of Cisco Sec=
ure Endpoint, the solution is positioned as Endpoint Detection and Response=
 (EDR), with integrated Extended Detection and Response (XDR) capabilities,=
 providing unified view, simplified incident management, and automated play=
books through the integration with Cisco XDR solutions.</p><div id=3D"ember=
90">         =20
  <figure class=3D"figure">
<!---->   =20
  <a href=3D"https://ondemandelearning.cisco.com/apollo-alpha/sec-scor-34-a=
mpforendpoints-20/assets/Security/Modular/SCOR/v2.0/Graphics/Course34/SCOR_=
2-0-0_Deploying_Cisco_AMP_for_Endpoints_What_You_Will_Learn_001.png" rel=3D=
"noopener noreferrer" target=3D"_blank" class=3D"transition-opacity hover:o=
pacity-75 focus:opacity-75">
    <img src=3D"https://ondemandelearning.cisco.com/apollo-alpha/sec-scor-3=
4-ampforendpoints-20/assets/Security/Modular/SCOR/v2.0/Graphics/Course34/SC=
OR_2-0-0_Deploying_Cisco_AMP_for_Endpoints_What_You_Will_Learn_001.png" cla=
ss=3D"figure-image max-h-[42cqi]">
  </a>

<!---->  </figure>

</div><p>By the end of this training, you will be able to describe the Cisc=
o Secure Endpoint architecture and the engines that it uses to detect threa=
ts. You will also be able to describe the security, device trajectory, and =
file trajectory features of Cisco Secure Endpoint. In addition, you will be=
 able to explain how Cisco Secure Endpoint is managed. Finally, you will be=
 able to configure policies and connectors for Cisco Secure Endpoint, use t=
he Cisco Secure Endpoint console to investigate and respond to security thr=
eats, and explain how Cisco Secure Endpoint detects ransomware and can bloc=
k an application from being executed.</p></div><!----><!----><!----><!---->=
